   \( 1 \text{ lb} = 0.4536 \text{ kg} \).  
   \( 32 \text{ lb} \times 0.4536 \text{ kg/lb} = 14.54 \text{ kg} \).

2. **Calculate the loading dose**:  
   \( 20 \text{ mg/kg} \times 14.54 \text{ kg} = 290.8 \text{ mg} \).

3. **Calculate the infusion time**:  
   \( 0.5 \text{ mg/kg/min} \times 14.54 \text{ kg} = 7.27 \text{ mg/min} \).  
   \( \text{Time} = \frac{290.8 \text{ mg}}{7.27 \text{ mg/min}} = 40.1 \text{ min} \).

