1. **Reaction with CO₂:** The Grignide ion (M⁻) from the Grignegen reacts with CO₂ to form a carboxylate ion.
   \[
   \text{Mg}^+} + \text{CO}_2 \rightarrow \text{Mg}^+ \text{COO}^-
   \]

2. **Deprotation:** The carboxylate ion is then protonated by adding an acid (e.g., HCl) to form the carboxylic acid.
   \[
   \text{Mg}^+ \text{COO}^- + \text{HCl} \rightarrow \text{COOH} + \text{MgCl}^-
   \]

