","When H₂S gas is passed into a mixture of Mn²⁺, Ni²⁺, Cu²⁺, and Hg²⁺ ions in an acidified aqueous solution, the following precipitates will form:  

1. **Copper sulfide (Cu₂S)**: Copper ions are highly reactive with H₂S.  
   \[ \text{Cu}^{2+} + 2\text{H}_2\text{S} \rightarrow \text{CuS} + 2\text{H}_2\text{O} \]  
   The precipitate is black.  

2. **Mercury sulfide (HgS)**: Mercury ions are also reactive with H₂S.  
   \[ \text{Hg}^{2+} + 2\text{H}_2\text{S} \rightarrow \text{HgS} + 2\text{H}_2\text{O} \]  
   The precipitate is black.  

3. **Magnesium sulfide (MgS)**: Magnesium ions are reactive with H₂S.  
   \[ \text{Mg}^{2+} + 2\text{H}_2\text{S} \rightarrow \text{MgS} + 2\text{H}_2\text{O} \]  
   The precipitate is white.  

Thus, the products are:  
- Copper sulfide (Cu₂S)  
- Mercury sulfide (HgS)  
- Magnesium sulfide (MgS)  

