A solution has a hydronium ion concentration \([H_3O^+]\) of \(10^{-4}\) M. What is the nature of this solution (acidic, basic, or neutral)?<end_of_turn>
<start_of_turn>model
","To determine the nature of the solution, we compare the \([H_3O^+]\) concentration to the \([OH^-]\) concentration. For a neutral solution, \([H_3O^+] = [OH^-] = 10^{-7}\) M at 25°C. 

1. **Calculate \([OH^-]\):**  
