","The bond between nitrogen (N) and oxygen (O) in NO2 is **polar**. This is because nitrogen and oxygen have different electronegativity values, leading to an uneven distribution of charge in the bond. Oxygen is more electronegative (0.54) than nitrogen (0.28), so it attracts electrons more strongly. This results in a slightly negatively charged oxygen (δ-) and a slightly positively charged nitrogen (δ+).  

