The reaction is as follows:  
\[ \text{Toluene} + \text{CCl}_2\text{Cl}_4 \rightarrow \text{Benzaldehyde} + \text{CCl}_4 + \text{HCl} \]  

**Key points:**  
- It is a selective oxidation process, specifically for converting aromatic hydrocarbons to their corresponding aldehydes.  
- The reaction is carried out in an organic solvent (e.g., chloroform) and at low temperatures (e.g., 0°C).  
- The reaction is highly sensitive to impurities and impurities can lead to the formation of other products (e.g., benzobenquinone).  

