   - Combine the results of these blocks sequentially in series or parallel, depending on the system's structure.  

**Final Answer:**  
The reliability function \( R_S(t) \) for the system is the product of the reliabilities of the series blocks and the complements of the products of the reliabilities of the parallel blocks.  

\[
R_S(t) = \boxed{1 - \prod_{i=1}^{n} (1 - R_i(t))}
\]  
for parallel systems and  
\[
R_S(t) = \boxed{\prod_{i=1}^{n} R_i(t)}
\]  
for series systems.  

