In summary, the possible types of isomerism in a molecule with the chemical formula C4H10O are structural isomerism (butanol isomers and diethyl ether) and stereoisomerism (optical isomerism in 2-butanol). The differences between these isomers lie in the arrangement of atoms and functional groups, as well as the spatial arrangement of atoms around chiral centers.
