   \[
   \text{Distance} = \text{total steps} \times \text{step length} = 1600 \text{ steps} \times 65 \text{ cm/step} = 104,000 \text{ cm} = 1040 \text{ m}
   \]

3. **Calculate Jack's steps per minute:**  
   \[
   \text{Jack's steps per minute} = 90 \text{ steps/min}
   \]

4. **Calculate Jack's step length:**  
   \[
   \text{Lisa's step length} = 55 \text{ cm/step}
   \]

5. **Calculate Julia's distance per minute:**  
   \[
   \text{Distance per minute} = \text{steps per minute} \times \text{step length} = 90 \text{ steps/min} \times 55 \text{ cm/step} = 4950 \text{ cm/min} = 49.5 \text{ m/min}
   \]

6. **Calculate how long it takes Julia to reach the house:**  
   \[
   \text{Time} = \frac{\text{Distance}}{\text{Distance per minute}} = \frac{1040 \text{ m}}{49.5 \text{ m/min}} = 21.02 \text{ min}
