<start_of_turn>model
","1. Convert speeds to meters per second:
   - Joger: \( 9 \text{ km/hr} = 9 \times \frac{1000}{3600} = 2.5 \text{ m/s} \)
   - Train: \( 45 \text{ km/hr} = 45 \times \frac{1000}{3600} = 12.5 \text{ m/s} \)

2. Calculate the relative speed:
   - The train is catching the joger, so the relative speed is the difference in their speeds: \( 12.5 - 2.5 = 10 \text{ m/s} \)

3. Calculate the distance the train must cover:
   - The train must cover the initial distance of 150 m to reach the jogge, then cover the length of the train to pass it.
   - The train takes 25 seconds to pass the joguer, so the distance covered in 25 seconds is: \( 150 + \text{Length of the train} \).
   - Using the relative speed and time: \( 10 \times 25 = 250 \text{ m} \)

4. Solve for the length of the train:
   - \( 250 = 150 + \text{Length of the train} \)
   - \( \text{Length of the train} = 250 - 150 = 100 \text{ m} \)

   The length of the train is \(\boxed{100 \text{ m}}\).",relevance,"# Task Description
