","1. **Calculate the distance a travels before b starts:**  
   \[
   \text{Distance} = \text{Speed} \times \text{Time} = 10 \text{ kmph} \times 3 \text{ h} = 30 \text{ km}
   \]

2. **Determine the relative speed of b relative to a:**  
   Since b is cycling at 20 kmph and a is running at 10 kmph, b is catching up at a rate of:  
   \[
   \text{Relative speed} = 20 \text{ kmph} - 10 \text{ kmph} = 10 \text{ kmph}
   \]

3. **Calculate the time it takes for b to catch up:**  
   B needs to cover the 30 km distance that a was away when b started.  
   \[
   \text{Time} = \frac{\text{Distance}}{\text{Relative speed}} = \frac{30 \text{ km}}{10 \text{ kmph}} = 3 \text{ h}
   \]

4. **Calculate the distance from the start when b catches up:**  
   Since b cycles at 20 kmph, the distance b travels in 3 hours is:  
   \[
   \text{Distance} = \text{Speed} \times \text{Time} = 20 \text{ kmph} \times 3 \text{ h} = 60 \text{ km}
   \]

   Therefore, b catches up with a at a distance of \(\boxed{60 \text{ km}}\) from the start.",fluency,"# Task Description
