\[
P_n(x) = \frac{1}{n!} \frac{d^n}{dx^n} \left( \left( \frac{1}{2} \right)^n \left( x^2 - 1 \right)^n \right).
\]
For \( n = 3 \), we have:
\[
P_3(x) = \frac{1}{3!} \frac{d^3}{dx^3} \left( \left( \frac{1}{2} \right)^3 \left( x^2 - 1 \right)^3 \right).
\]
First, compute the derivative:
\[
\left( \frac{1}{2} \right)^3 \left( x^2 - 1 \right)^3 = \frac{1}{8} \left( x^2 - 1 \right)^3 = \frac{1}{8} \left( x^6 - 3x^4 + 3x^2 - 1 \right).
\]
Differentiate once:
\[
\frac{d}{dx} \left( \frac{1}{8} \left( x^6 - 3x^4 + 3x^2 - 1 \right) \right) = \frac{1}{8} \left( 6x^5 - 12x^3 + 6x \right).
\]
Differentiate again:
\[
\frac{d}{dx} \left( \frac{1}{8} \left( 6x^5 - 12x^3 + 6x \right) \right) = \frac{1}{8} \left( 30x^4 - 36x^2 + 6 \right).
\]
