The index of refraction (n) of a material is defined as the ratio of the speed of light in a vacuum (c) to the speed of light in the medium (v):

n = c / v

In this case, the speed of light in the plastic (v) is 0.680 times the speed of light in a vacuum (c). So, v = 0.680c.

n = c / (0.680c)

The c terms cancel out, leaving:

