   \]  
   \[
   \text{Strands per m}^2 = 1 \text{ strand per cm}^2 \times (100 \text{ cm per m})^2 = 10,000 \text{ strands per m}^2
   \]  
   The number of strands per square meter is 10,000.

2. **Calculate the wetted area of each strand**:  
   The wetted area of a single strand is:  
   \[
   \text{Wetted area per strand} = \text{Length of strand} \times \text{Diameter of strand}
   \]  
   The length of the strand is 1 m (since the net is 1 m² and the squares are 1 cm²).  
   \[
   \text{Wetted area per strand} = 1 \text{ m} \times 0.001 \text{ m} = 0.001 \text{ m}^2
   \]  

3. **Calculate the total wetted area of the net**:  
   \[
   \text{Total wetted area} = \text{Strands per m}^2 \times \text{Wetted area per strand} = 10,000 \times 0.001 \text{ m}^2 = 10 \text{ m}^2
   \]  

