5. Encapsulation and passivation: Plasma treatment can be used to create protective coatings on the surface of solar cells, which can protect the solar cell from environmental degradation, such as UV radiation and moisture. This can help to improve the long-term stability and lifetime of the solar cell.

In summary, plasma-based nanotechnology can be used to improve the efficiency and lifetime of solar cells by improving light absorption, carrier collection, and environmental degradation. This can lead to more efficient and long-lasting solar cells, which can help to make solar energy a more attractive energy source.
