\[
KE = \frac{1}{2} m v^2 = \frac{1}{2} \times 400 \times (800)^2 = 128 \times 10^6 \, \text{J} = 128 \, \text{MJ}
\]

The kinetic energy of the satellite is \(\boxed{128 \, \text{MJ}}\).
